    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d434">

                <pb facs="0601" n="505" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg505"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">431.12/2¾: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Mexico</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Summerlin</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-10-11T11:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 11,
                                1921—11 a.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>132. Embassy’s telegrams no. 190, dated October 8, noon, and no. 189 October 4, 5
                        p.m.<anchor n="31" xml:id="d434-f1"/> The Department is now studying
                    decision of Supreme Court<anchor n="32" xml:id="d434-f2"/> received several days
                    ago, and additional <pb facs="0602" n="506" xml:id="pg506"/> instructions will
                    be forwarded shortly. Any suggestions which Señor Pani desires to make will be
                    gladly received by Department.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d434-f1" n="31" xml:id="d434-f1-content">
                <p>The latter not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d434-f2" n="32" xml:id="d434-f2-content">
                <p>Decision of the Mexican Supreme Court, Aug. 30, 1921, in the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">amparo</hi> case of the Texas Co. of Mexico, <ref
                        target="#pg461">pp. 461</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
